From 37470438645d7bd752cdc47f4474594428543046 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 14:03:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci(item-2b): wire --check-followup into CI, adopt TOL=1e-8
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

item2b_determinism_report.md §5 resolved: torch.use_deterministic_algorithms(True,
warn_only=True) is confirmed present in run_comparative_suite_benchmark_v2.py
(commit e5e33ee, predating run 31312938979) and fires no fallback warnings, so
the residual 3.37e-10 Snell's Law spread on EHD/M3 is the accepted
floating-point reduction-order floor, not an unaddressed nondeterminism
source. Both open items from the report are now closed:

- .github/scripts/run_issue2b_experiment.sh: new HSL_PATH/EHD_PATH env vars
  (auto-resolved from the harness's repo root), a "Preflight: follow-up patch
  check" step that runs --check-followup right after the existing
  --check-patch step and aborts (exit 2) on failure, and TOL default changed
  0.0 -> 1e-8 per the report's §6 recommendation.

- .github/workflows/ci_issue2b_repro.yml: new hsl_path/ehd_path workflow
  inputs; --check-followup now runs inside the dry_run preflight and as an
  unconditional gate before every real Phase A/B dispatch; tol input default
  changed 0.0 -> 1e-8.

- item2b_determinism_report.md: updated to reflect the above -- §5 rewritten
  from open question to resolved, §6 recommendation marked adopted, §3/§7
  CI-wiring action item marked done, plus a new §8 explaining why
  determinism matters for this benchmark specifically (method comparison
  validity, noise-sweep baseline stability, the three independent randomness
  sources HSL/EHD each stack, and regression-test attributability).

No change to run_comparative_suite_benchmark_v2.py or the HSL/EHD domain
modules themselves -- this commit only wires up and documents checks against
code that was already correct.
